On the wide rocky beach below the towering grey cliff of the Herbstfelsen, Emma, a little girl with brown wavy ear-length hair in a ponytail with a side part, brown eyes, freckles, wearing a red knitted wool sweater, black denim leggings, and yellow rubber rain boots, stands facing right on the pebbled shore with her hands pressed flat against her chest, clutching a shiny dark brown chestnut with a tan patch, her lips rounded in a soft hum as she gazes down at the smooth seed. Beside her in the foreground, Noah, a little boy with blonde wavy ear-length hair with bangs at his eyebrows, blue eyes, dressed in a yellow hooded sweatshirt, brown corduroy trousers, and brown leather ankle boots, stands facing right, watching Emma's hands with wide eyes and his hands tucked into his sweatshirt pocket. High above on a flat rocky outcrop of the dry cliff wall in the background, Hans, an elderly man with short straight brushed-back white hair, a white handlebar mustache, small moles on his right cheek and left forehead, dressed in a grey loden wool jacket, a white collared cotton shirt, brown woollen trousers, sturdy brown leather walking shoes, and a brown flat wool cap, sits looking out across the vast dark water with empty hands resting open on his knees, his lips slightly parted as he hums the matching tune into the autumn afternoon air, dry golden leaves scattered across the rocky shoreline below.

---METADATA---
