Seen from an over-the-shoulder perspective behind Sarah, where only the back of her head with straight chin-length blonde hair, the wide lapels and shoulder of her long purple wool coat, and the collar of her cream-white turtleneck are visible in the corner of the frame, Sarah stands at the edge of the flat, wet grey stones looking out toward the evening water. Out in the calm sea just beyond the lowest stone, the sea turtle Kora breaks the surface of the dark water, her deep olive-green patterned head lifted smoothly, gentle brown eyes open wide beneath a level brow, her soft rounded beak closed, and the domed tan and dark brown segmented shell gleaming as evening light catches the gentle ripples in the autumn dusk.

---METADATA---
