In a wide view of the shadowy underwater expanse, sweeping directional ocean currents churn through dense clouds of black ink that drift across the dark blue reef. The large sea turtle Kora, her deep olive-green flippers sweeping wide against the pulling flow and her tan and dark brown segmented shell tilted in the current, turns facing right across the dim water, her gentle brown eyes open wide with concern and her rounded beak firmly closed as she searches the ink-filled void where the children have vanished from sight.

---METADATA---
