Floating alone in the close-up framing of the murky, ink-clouded water, Emma, a little girl with brown wavy ear-length hair in a ponytail with a side part, brown eyes, freckles, wearing a long-sleeve shimmering green scale-patterned top and a shimmering green mermaid tail with a wide fanned fin, faces right with her hands open at her sides, her head tilted slightly back and her mouth rounded in a clear, resonant hum. From a narrow vertical crack in the coral reef wall beside her, a gentle, warm golden light begins to glow, answering the song into the dark autumn sea.

