Near the towering purple and blue coral archway on the sandy reef floor, Emma, a little girl with brown wavy ear-length hair in a ponytail with a side part, brown eyes, freckles, wearing a long-sleeve shimmering green scale-patterned top and a shimmering green mermaid tail with a wide fanned fin, extends her right hand flat and open toward Oskar, presenting the shiny dark brown chestnut on her palm with a gentle, trusting expression. Floating opposite her, the reddish-orange octopus Oskar, his round blue eyes wide with delight and mouth softly rounded, unfurls his eight flexible arms completely from the glowing pearlescent singing shell necklace to wrap two delicate tentacles around the round chestnut, allowing the singing shell to drift free into the calm water.

