On the wide autumn shoreline where the wet stepping stones meet the pebbled beach, Daniel, a middle-aged man with short wavy dark brown hair, a short beard, brown eyes, dressed in a blue waterproof rain jacket, black trousers, and black waterproof hiking boots, stands firmly on the large safe stone in the foreground, grinning with deep relief as he lifts Emma and Noah up out of the dark water gap. Emma, a little girl with brown wavy ear-length hair in a ponytail, brown eyes, freckles, wearing a red knitted wool sweater, black denim leggings, yellow rubber rain boots, and the pearlescent white singing shell necklace hanging securely around her neck, smiles up at Daniel with joyful relief, while Noah, a little boy with blonde wavy ear-length hair, blue eyes, in a yellow hooded sweatshirt, brown corduroy trousers, and brown leather ankle boots, holds Daniel's arm as his boots reach the stone. Beside them, Sarah, an adult woman with chin-length straight blonde hair, rectangular black-framed glasses, blue eyes, wearing a long purple wool coat over a cream-white turtleneck sweater, dark grey jeans, and brown leather ankle boots, steps forward with outstretched arms and a broad relieved smile under the fading dusk sky.

