In a close-up on the weathered stone ledge high on the Herbstfelsen, Emma, a little girl with brown wavy ear-length hair in a ponytail with a side part, brown eyes, freckles, wearing a red knitted wool sweater and black denim leggings, stands facing left and gently lays the glowing pearlescent singing shell necklace into the cupped, open hands of Hans. Hans, an elderly man with short brushed-back white hair, a white handlebar mustache, small moles on his right cheek and left forehead, dressed in a grey loden wool jacket, white collared shirt, and a brown flat wool cap, cradles the glowing shell with trembling fingers, his brown eyes glistening with quiet wonder and his lips rounded in a soft hum as the warm light of the shell hums Mira's melody back to him in the autumn dusk.

